<P><FONT SIZE=+1><B>Travel</B></FONT>

<P><B>Directions to OU: </B> Oakland University extends into two cities - Auburn Hills and Rochester Hills, between Adams Road and Squirrel Road, just south of Walton Boulevard. Take I-75 to exit 79 and go east on University Drive to the main entrance of campus. Or, take M-59 to the Squirrel Road exit and go north to the main entrance of campus at the corner of University Drive. Please click here for detailed information on 
<A HREF="http://www2.oakland.edu/map/">Directions and the Campus map. </A> 

<P>You would fly to the Detroit Metro Airport and catch a shuttle from there. Most hotels do have shuttle service to the airport. Other options are to fly to Oakland Airport, Toledo, or Windsor. 



<P><FONT SIZE=+1><B>Accommodations</B></FONT>



<P>There are many places near OU's campus for visitors:

<P><B>Dorms:  </B>

A few dorm rooms will be available.  They are not air conditioned.

<P>Prices

<LI>$18 per person, per night, double occupancy (no linens, maid service, or food)
<LI>$24.50 per person, per night single 9no linens, maid service, or food)

<P>with linens (this includes linens but no maid service and no food.)

<LI> $31.50 per person, per night, double occupancy</LI>
<LI>$39.50 per person, per night, single occupancy</LI>

<P> For more information or booking the rooms please contact: 
<A HREF="http://www4.oakland.edu/?sid=3"> Housing and Dining</A>  You can send an email to housing@oakland.edu  or call 248-370-3570


<P><B>Hotels</B>

